<%# The brand: "$plit", drawn twice and cut across the middle. The top copy is
    clipped to its upper half and the bottom copy to its lower half, then each is
    nudged sideways in CSS, so the logo is literally split. Two copies of live
    text (rather than an image) keep it in the app's font and let the nav and
    the intro share one definition. Both copies are hidden from screen readers;
    the link or overlay that holds this names the app. %>
<span class="wordmark-art" aria-hidden="true">
  <span class="wordmark-half wordmark-half--top"><span>$</span>plit</span>
  <span class="wordmark-half wordmark-half--bottom"><span>$</span>plit</span>
</span>
